sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Admin or Coordinator
    participant FE as Web app
    participant BA as batch-service
    participant K as Kafka
    participant CR as course-service
    participant NO as notification-service

    Note over A,BA: Extend a whole batch
    A->>FE: Extend course on the batch page, new end date and the reason
    FE->>BA: POST /api/batches/{id}/extend
    BA->>BA: STAFF only, the date must be later, a cancelled batch cannot be extended
    BA->>BA: set the end date, a COMPLETED batch becomes ONGOING again
    BA->>BA: students whose own access date was the old end date follow it, expired ones are on the course again
    BA->>K: notification.requested (students of the batch and the trainer)
    K->>NO: tell them the new date and the reason
    BA->>K: audit.recorded (BATCH_EXTENDED with the reason)

    Note over A,BA: Set or extend one student
    A->>FE: Set date, Extend or Reopen beside the student on the roster
    FE->>BA: POST /api/batches/enrollments/{id}/access
    BA->>BA: only an active or expired student, the date cannot be in the past
    alt the access had run out (EXPIRED)
        BA->>BA: refuse if the student is already on this course in another batch
        BA->>BA: status ACTIVE again
        BA->>K: enrollment.created
        K->>CR: open the course mirror again, progress kept
    end
    BA->>K: notification.requested (your access is extended until the date)
    BA->>K: audit.recorded (ACCESS_EXTENDED)

    Note over BA,CR: Every night at 01:20
    BA->>BA: ACTIVE enrolments whose access date has passed become EXPIRED
    BA->>K: enrollment.closed, and notify the student
    K->>CR: lock the course for that student
    Note over BA: an enrolment with no access date is never touched
